  "description": "A parametric FAUCET on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nA TAP EXISTS SEPARATELY because the basin and the sink each carry one, and neither can serve a wall mixer, a bath filler or a second tap on a double bowl. This is that object: a body, a spout that reaches, and one or two handles.\n\nMOUNT MOVES THE SPOUT, not the shape. A Deck mixer puts the spout at the top of the body; a Wall mixer drops it to a fifth of the way up and shortens the body to a wall plate; a Pillar tap adds the second handle. One ternary each, no second flow.\n\nSPOUT REACH AND LEVEL ARE PUBLISHED because they are the two numbers that decide whether a tap clears the bowl it is over — and neither is legible in a plan, where a tap is a few centimetres of nothing.",
